# Settings of the personal (local) AgenticWF container: install as ~/.agenticwf/local.env, which
# compose.local.yaml reads (or pass it with `docker run --env-file`). Recreate the container after
# changing it. Models and other agent/KB settings: README.md, Local use.

# Which services: "agent kb" (default), "agent" or "kb". The same variable in the shell wins.
# AGENTICWF_SERVICES=agent kb
# Your login; the subject of everything you add is local:<login> in both services. Default: your
# login on the host (compose); the same variable in the shell wins.
# AGENTICWF_LOCAL_USER=agenticwf
# A phrase of yours (at least 8 characters): the sign-in pages of the agent and the KB show the
# token to whoever gives it, so treat it like a password. Wrong answers are throttled (after 5,
# one try a minute). Unset: get the token with the commands the pages show (agenticwf-links).
# AGENTICWF_LOCAL_HINT=
# The container's name, for the commands the sign-in pages show (default: its id).
# AGENTICWF_CONTAINER=agenticwf
# The name the agent shows for you.
# AGENT_LOCAL_NAME=Agentic WF

# Model provider keys for the agent (agent.cfg [llm]; mount your own agent.cfg to add models) and
# web search. Keys added on the agent's admin page are stored encrypted in its database instead.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# The KB's access token instead of a generated one (at least 16 characters).
# KB_TOKEN=
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Traces to Jaeger (compose.jaeger.yaml) on this machine; host.docker.internal is Docker Desktop's
# name for it. Don't set OTEL_SERVICE_NAME (the agent and the KB name themselves).
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:4318
